{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AkC2uDSrfW3QTF3V7Kke6x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user productivity + R&D mission-control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, markdown as source of truth, Python stdlib only save for one declared `pywinpty` exception).\n\n- **Core purpose â€” a task/project manager backed by plain markdown.** Tasks and projects live in human-readable files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files under `domains/`). Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done/cancelled/saved â†’ restored), and everything is editable by CLI, browser, or any text tool.\n\n- **What it ships as the primary app â€” `anchor_gui.py`.** A self-contained stdlib HTTP server (the one declared deliverable) that renders the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes back to the markdown files via `/api/*` endpoints. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` bound to `http://localhost:8777`.\n\n- **A CLI mirror â€” `anchor.py`.** Same logic and file format as the GUI, plus it generates the static `dashboard.html` and mirrors the R&D data/inspection commands (`anchor.py rnd â€¦`).\n\n- **An R&D \"cockpit\" layered on top (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4, all built/merged).** Each project gets a window where the Research â†’ Planning â†’ Build \"trio\" (researchPrime Â· Crucible Â· Foreman skills) runs as durable, isolated, server-side terminal sessions. v3 added real ConPTY terminals with per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, cached project/session summaries, stage handoffs, and runnable deliverable previews (guarded off port 8777). v4 (\"Project Cockpit\") turned it into lane tiles with status lights and inline expanding panels, a skill-auto-load-once terminal, a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, and cost/tokens/time rollups.\n\n- **Self-verifying.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and walks the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (never the live service or real `claude`), writing a dated report to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool** \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark.\n\nThese claims are grounded in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North Stars from the rnd-v3/v4 planning docs. The one caveat worth flagging: the documents describe the v4 surface as built and merged (`38fd70e`), but the gitStatus snapshot shows uncommitted changes to dashboard/markdown files â€” so the *working tree* is ahead of the last described commit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0369ec16-cc98-4f52-be15-a8b610c2856c","uuid":"f5689cf0-c581-4dec-96ba-4f706b76d391","request_id":"req_011Cc1fXcSSLRcbmxWUSHChz"}
